\end{aligned}
$$

Since $\lim _{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{n}{\sqrt{n^{2}+n}+n}=\lim _{n \rightarrow \infty} \frac{1}{\sqrt{1+\frac{1}{n}}+1}=\frac{1}{2}$, we get $\lim _{n \rightarrow \infty} a_{n}=\sin ^{2} \frac{\pi}{2}=1$.

