\]

After expanding and combining the terms, this is equivalent to \(4 r_{1}^{2}=8 r_{1} \sqrt{r_{2} r_{3}}\) and thus

\[
r_{1}^{2}=4 r_{2} r_{3} \Rightarrow r_{3}=\frac{r_{1}^{2}}{4 r_{2}}
\]

